{"author":{"id":"1832e4168d45d4ef31531146dbc743bb950a5dd543b15fd8e3a076fd976bfdef"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790983456,"nonce":"YYyK8A7bPkLUXPFYab5L8+rs9eA=","title":"a method argument cannot be an optional enum","message":"`fn setTheme(this: \u0026Window, theme: Option\u003cEnum\u003cTheme\u003e\u003e)` is refused with \"unsupported argument type in Window.setTheme\". xwindow needs it for winit's `Window::set_theme(Option\u003cTheme\u003e)` (xwindow git-bug 326e773cd8e4abecfb15dca502bdaf0f68834248285023de1125093b8236cde9): none means follow the system's theme, distinct from either value, so an extra enum member would only stand in for it. `Option\u003cEnum\u003cT\u003e\u003e` already works as a record field (WindowAttributes.theme), not as a method argument.\n\nWanted on Caribou, HashLink/Ash and Rayzor, with the Haxe surfaces taking `?theme:Theme`. Asked for by the xwindow session, 2026-10-03.","files":null}]}